    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\n- [x] 1. Forcefully close file window (**not planned**, see https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1506#issuecomment-2603187976)\n\nYou can use instead https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1506#issuecomment-2604024475\n\n```lua\nMiniFiles.close { force = true }\n```\n\n```lua\n-- Default\nMiniFiles.config = {\n  mappings = {\n    close_force = '',\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n- [x] 2. Add a configuration option to automatically remove the `modified` state when reaching `Already at oldest change` (**done**, implemented in a different way, see https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1506#issuecomment-2603187976)\n\n```lua\n-- Default\nMiniFiles.config = {\n  modified_at_oldest = true,\n}\n```\n\nI am a simple person: I press undo 20 times and then close the window.\n\n---\n\n- [x] 3. ~I would not exit `modified` window before the actual confirmation.~ (**expected**, see https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1506#issuecomment-2603064071)\n\nYou can use instead https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1506#issuecomment-2604024475\n\nKeep in mind that I am closing the window via `:q` and then choosing (No).\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5cfc8107-7165-4993-8a94-cd3a9cd11a3f\n",
