            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Sorry for the messy issue. These are actually three different suggestions within the related category.\n\n`[1]` - Feature 1\n`[2]` - Feature 2\n`[3]` - ~Bug. I closed the window using the `:quit` command~ (non-relevant, see [your previous comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1506#issuecomment-2603064071))\n\nWhen I modify the buffer and undo to the initial state (when there are no changes), I still need to confirm before exiting (see feature `[2]`).\nAnd in case I just want to exit regardless of any changes without confirmation, it would be nice to have feature `[1]`.\n\nAs you can see, implementing feature `[1]` would resolve feature `[2]`. However, I thought it would be nice to show that there are no changes left in the buffer if we undo enough.\n\nOr maybe for feature `[2]`, the option should only remove the highlight, or there should be an event to fire that allows the user to remove the highlight.",
