            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the clarification.\n\nI believe having a confirmation after *any* text change is important as it draws attention to something that can potentially modify file system (which can potentially be an irreversible change). So force closing is out of scope.\n\nThe suggestion 2 might be reasonable, but slightly on another level by replacing check for modified buffer with the check for \"pending\" file system actions. As there are none for after undos and some other situations (like adding empty lines), those will allow closing explorer without confirmation. I'll take a look.",
