        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "From my standpoint, I think `[1]` is reasonable because the user *cannot* write anything to the file system without synchronizing it first. This option simply allows closing the window and discarding any potential changes.\n\nIf the buffer is modified, the plugin displays a pop-up message like:\n - Do you really want to close the window? `[Yes]/[No]`\n - Drop all changes? `[Yes]/[No]`\n - Exit without saving? `[Yes]/[No]`\n\nWith this option we can choose `Yes` by default and ignore potential changes to the file system (like `:qa!`).\n\nMost importantly, to draw the user's attention, this option may only exist as an argument to `MiniFiles.close()`. This means that the user needs to define it separately (except when they copy-paste the config from somewhere else).\n\nAlso, features `[1]` and `[2]` can be combined in different ways:\n  - remove/change highlight if it's the oldest change **and** exit without confirmation\n  - or only remove/change highlight if it's the oldest change **but** exit with confirmation, because a different keymap can be set to exit without confirmation\n\n---\n\nIn any case, I am glad that you considered the issue and will be happy with any outcome, even if no changes are made.\nGreat thanks for your work ❤️",
