            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I will share here how to forcefully close the window. It is not that hard for the user to implement.\n\n---\n\nFeature `[1]`\n\n<details><summary>Force close <code>mini.files</code> using <code>vim.fn.feedkeys</code> (emulates user typing, <b>causes message jump</b>)</summary>\n\n```lua\nlocal files_close_force = function()\n  -- You can omit schedule if you really want\n  vim.schedule(function()\n    vim.fn.feedkeys('Y', 'n')\n  end)\n  files.close()\nend\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details open><summary>Force close <code>mini.files</code> by mocking <code>vim.fn.confirm</code> (relies on implementation details)</summary>\n\n```lua\nlocal files_close_force = function()\n  local fn_confirm = vim.fn.confirm\n  vim.fn.confirm = function() ---@diagnostic disable-line: duplicate-set-field\n    return 1\n  end\n  files.close()\n  vim.fn.confirm = fn_confirm\nend\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\nBug `[3]`\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> The bug applies only to `modified` windows.\n\n<details><summary>Force close <code>mini.files</code> on <code>:quit</code></summary>\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('QuitPre', {\n  callback = function()\n    if vim.bo.ft == 'minifiles' then\n      files_close_force()\n    end\n  end,\n})\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details open><summary>Force close <code>mini.files</code> on <code>:quit</code> only if the leftmost window is focused.\n\nIt hides the current window and all its branches\n</summary>\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('QuitPre', {\n  callback = function()\n    if vim.bo.ft == 'minifiles' then\n      files.go_out()\n      files.trim_right()\n    end\n  end,\n})\n```\n\n</details>\n\n",
